text:
{
  "opening": "This release introduces support for several new locales and corrects critical issues in timezone handling and humanization formatting. Maintainers must ensure that all new locale classes are properly exposed and that existing behavior remains stable for users relying on current APIs.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "The public API must expose the OdiaLocale class under the name OdiaLocale. The MalayLocale class must remain accessible under the name MalayLocale."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "The ArrowFactory.get method must correctly handle the tzinfo keyword argument when passed with datetime, Arrow, date, or iso_calendar objects. The behavior of ArrowFactory.get must be consistent and clear regarding timezone application across all supported input types."
    },
    {
      "id": "m04",
      "text": "The public API must expose the MalteseLocale class under the name MalteseLocale. The MalayLocale and OdiaLocale classes must remain accessible under their respective names."
    },
    {
      "id": "m07",
      "text": "The TurkishLocale class must be available under the name TurkishLocale with updated translation data reflecting the latest locale standards."
    },
    {
      "id": "m08",
      "text": "The public API must expose the SerbianLocale class under the name SerbianLocale. The OdiaLocale class must remain accessible under the name OdiaLocale."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "The public API must expose the SamiLocale class under the name SamiLocale. The MalteseLocale and OdiaLocale classes must remain accessible under their respective names."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10",
      "text": "The public API must expose the LuxembourgishLocale class under the name LuxembourgishLocale. The SerbianLocale class must remain accessible under the name SerbianLocale, and the describe function must continue to operate as expected."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "Humanize output must not display floating-point numbers when a locale class overrides _format_timeframe. The Locale base class and HebrewLocale must behave such that timeframes are formatted as integers or appropriate string representations without float artifacts."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify that all new locales integrate seamlessly with the existing humanization and factory mechanisms. Ensure no regressions occur in timezone-aware object creation."
}
